oiler steam, so a large steam exporter can show a total below zero.","grid_kg_kwh":0.213},"greener":{"title":"Green methanol and CO2 based CO","text":"Almost all the carbon footprint sits in the methanol and CO feeds. Methanol from captured CO2 and green hydrogen, and CO from CO2 by reverse shift or electrolysis, give a near zero carbon acid from the same plant."},"hazards":[{"id":"MeOH","name":"Methanol","formula":"CH3OH","cas":"67-56-1","ghs":[{"code":"H225","text":"Highly flammable liquid and vapour"},{"code":"H301","text":"Toxic if swallowed"},{"code":"H311","text":"Toxic in contact with skin"},{"code":"H331","text":"Toxic if inhaled"},{"code":"H370","text":"Causes damage to organs"}],"severe":true,"flash_point_C":9,"autoignition_C":440,"LFL_pct":6.0,"UFL_pct":36.0,"Tb_C":64},{"id":"CO","name":"Carbon monoxide","formula":"CO","cas":"630-08-0","ghs":[{"code":"H220","text":"Extremely flammable gas"},{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"},{"code":"H331","text":"Toxic if inhaled"},{"code":"H360D","text":"May damage the unborn child"},{"code":"H372","text":"Causes damage to organs through prolonged or repeated exposure"}],"severe":true,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":607,"LFL_pct":10.9,"UFL_pct":74.0,"Tb_C":-192},{"id":"H2","name":"Hydrogen","formula":"H2","cas":"1333-74-0","ghs":[{"code":"H220","text":"Extremely flammable gas"},{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"}],"severe":true,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":560,"LFL_pct":4.0,"UFL_pct":77.0,"Tb_C":-253},{"id":"AcOH","name":"Acetic acid","formula":"C2H4O2","cas":"64-19-7","ghs":[{"code":"H226","text":"Flammable liquid and vapour"},{"code":"H314","text":"Causes severe skin burns and eye damage"}],"severe":true,"flash_point_C":39,"autoignition_C":510,"LFL_pct":4.0,"UFL_pct":19.9,"Tb_C":118},{"id":"CH4","name":"Methane","formula":"CH4","cas":"74-82-8","ghs":[{"code":"H220","text":"Extremely flammable gas"},{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"}],"severe":true,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":600,"LFL_pct":4.4,"UFL_pct":17.0,"Tb_C":-161},{"id":"N2","name":"Nitrogen","formula":"N2","cas":"7727-37-9","ghs":[{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"},{"code":"ASPH","text":"Simple asphyxiant in confined spaces"}],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":-196},{"id":"CO2","name":"Carbon dioxide","formula":"CO2","cas":"124-38-9","ghs":[{"code":"H280","text":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"},{"code":"ASPH","text":"Simple asphyxiant in confined spaces"}],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":-78},{"id":"H2O","name":"Water","formula":"H2O","cas":"7732-18-5","ghs":[],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":100}],"hazop":[{"node":"CO compressor and feed","deviation":"Loss of containment","cause":"Seal or flange failure","consequence":"Toxic carbon monoxide release (no smell), fire","safeguard":"CO detectors, dry gas seals, ventilated compressor house, remote isolation"},{"node":"Reactor","deviation":"Low CO partial pressure","cause":"CO supply trip","consequence":"Catalyst precipitates and is lost, corrosion rises","safeguard":"CO flow and pressure trips, catalyst stabiliser, low water control"},{"node":"Reactor and flash","deviation":"Wrong material or water upset","cause":"Repairs in the wrong alloy, high iodide or water","consequence":"Rapid iodide corrosion and leaks of hot acid","safeguard":"Positive material identification, zirconium or Hastelloy, corrosion coupons"},{"node":"Acid storage","deviation":"Release","cause":"Tank or hose failure","consequence":"Corrosive, flammable above 39 C","safeguard":"Bunds, nitrogen blanket, PPE, safety showers"}],"process_hazards":[{"hazard":"Pressure","detail":"Up to 30 bar. Relief valves sized for fire and blocked outlet."},{"hazard":"Flammable materials","detail":"Methanol, Carbon monoxide, Hydrogen, Acetic acid, Methane. Hazardous area classification, ignition source control, gas detection, fire protection."},{"hazard":"Toxic materials","detail":"Methanol, Carbon monoxide. Toxic gas detection, emergency shutdown and isolation, escape sets, minimise inventory."},{"hazard":"Corrosive materials","detail":"Acetic acid. Material selection, PPE, safety showers, bunded storage."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Selectivity on methanol","model":99.5,"published":99,"unit":"%","error_pct":0.505051,"inside_range":null,"source":"Jones (BP Chemicals), The Cativa Process for the Manufacture of Acetic Acid, Platinum Metals Review 44(3), 2000","url":"https://technology.matthey.com/article/44/3/94-105/","note":"Jones gives greater than 99% for the rhodium process and the Cativa process is at least as good. The model value follows from the assumed methane and by-product loss, so this confirms the input only.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":1,"pass":true},{"metric":"CO utilisation, Cativa","model":92.337443,"published":94,"unit":"%","error_pct":-1.768678,"inside_range":null,"source":"Jones (BP Chemicals), The Cativa Process for the Manufacture of Acetic Acid, Platinum Metals Review 44(3), 2000","url":"https://technology.matthey.com/article/44/3/94-105/","note":"Jones: about 85% for Monsanto, above 94% for Cativa. Model loss = shift reaction plus CO carried out with the vent at the assumed head space partial pressures.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":true},{"metric":"CO per t acetic acid","model":0.50615,"published":0.47,"unit":"t/t","error_pct":7.691452,"inside_range":null,"source":"Credence Research, Carbon Monoxide Plant Project Report 2026","url":"https://www.credenceresearch.com/plant-projects/carbon-monoxide-manufacturing-plant-project-report","note":"Contained CO only. The stoichiometric minimum is 0.466 t/t, so 0.47 implies about 99% CO utilisation, above the 94% Jones gives for Cativa; the model follows Jones and reads high here.","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":5,"pass":false},{"metric":"Fixed capital, scaled from published project","model":63102359.576601,"published":329527931.973583,"unit":"USD (2024)","error_pct":-80.85068,"inside_range":null,"source":"Chemwin news (April 2024): Shenghong Refining and Chemical, Lianyungang, 1,000,000 t/y acetic acid, total investment CNY 3,852 million including PSA hydrogen, low-temperature methanol wash and cryogenic CO units. Converted at 7.1957 CNY/USD (US Federal Reserve G.5A, 2024 average), exponent 0.7","url":"https://en.888chem.com/news/2/20955.html","note":"The published total includes making the CO from syngas, which this model buys over the fence, and is a Chinese build cost; the model is a US grassroots Turton estimate.","kind":"capex","tolerance_pct":50,"pass":false}],"assumptions":["Catalyst metals, methyl iodide and methyl acetate stay inside the reactor, flash and light ends loop and are not shown as streams; the catalyst solution recycle is counted as acetic acid.","Carbon monoxide comes over the fence from a cryogenic cold box at 98.5% CO, with hydrogen and nitrogen.","Shift reaction makes 0.010 mol CO2 per mol acid and 0.5% of the methanol goes to methane and lumped by-products such as propionic acid (assumed).","CO lost with the vent follows from the inerts and by-product gases at an assumed 8 bar CO and 4 bar other gases in the reactor head space.","Reactor and flash vessel are zirconium in practice; the cost method only has carbon and stainless steel, so they are costed as stainless steel and the capital reads low.","Jones reports steam and cooling water about 30% below the rhodium process but no absolute figure, so steam is not checked against a number.","The HP vent is burnt in the site boiler in place of gas; its CO2 counts as direct emissions."],"notes":[]}